# GitHub Linguist language-statistics correction
# ffi_win.inc is generated code for the in-house Windows FFI ABI wrapper (1705 static wrapper functions, 515KB),
# and Linguist reads the .inc suffix as C++, which made the language bar report 57% C++; marking it generated keeps it out of the statistics.
internal/lang/ffi_win.inc linguist-generated=true

# Compiled artefacts: excluded from diffs
compiler/qkc binary

# The authored message tables are the input to the generated catalog in internal/i18n. Pin them to LF in
# every checkout: a CRLF working tree would otherwise put a carriage return inside a message's text on
# Windows and make the generator's output platform-dependent. (The syntax layer pins the same pattern.)
internal/i18n/source/*.tsv text eol=lf
